  "interpretation": [
    "The declared445 request pool has a measured no-pending-request interval after all pre3600 requests insert and before the first h4 request. This concerns the modeled boundary input, not unseen real upstream traffic.",
    "The delay stages use actual insertion, native ordinary-road exitTimes and E1 notification times. Each exit-to-exit stage includes the intervening internal connection and moving travel; it cannot be called stopped waiting on that ordinary road.",
    "All nine added counter requests contribute in the first window, while original h4 primary contributions decrease202 to193. This is an observed allocation change under the same recorded colors, not a capacity bound or a marginal assignment matrix.",
    "No per-vehicle lane-position/FCD timeline is present in these full outputs. Exact stopping position, lane changes, instantaneous leader and the signal responsible for each road interval remain unknown.",
    "The boundary no-pending-demand interval does appear downstream as41.9s without445 exits and40.9s without761 exits, but no full separation of old/new request cohorts remains at199#0 or244. Buffered old vehicles continue beyond the first h4 vehicle there.",
    "This is not a claim thatLSA119 has no cars or reaches capacity. The entry request gap and later internal delays are distinct observations; no new timing or demand candidate is generated."
  ],
